/Subject (The SPIDER dataset paper\072 a large publicly available multi\055centre lumbar spine MRI dataset with reference segmentations of vertebrae\054 intervertebral discs and spinal canal \055 447 sagittal T1 and T2 series from 218 patients with a history of low back pain\054 collected across four hospitals\054 and combined with per\055level radiological gradings\056 Annotation was iterative\072 a segmentation algorithm trained on a small subset produced initial masks that were reviewed\054 manually corrected and fed back into training\056 Reference performance is given for that baseline algorithm and for nnU\055Net\054 which performed comparably\054 computed on a sequestered set of 39 studies \05097 series\051 that also underpins a continuous public segmentation challenge for fair algorithm comparison\056 The major public lumbar MRI segmentation resource \055 and the dataset several other records here build on \055 so it must be discussed before segmentation can be dismissed as future work\056)
